ng the blockers. Never set a file aside on the strength of an empty MLB entry or a missing, false, or unreadable decision alone, because a private lock can precede its decision and successful delivery can precede its durable acknowledgement or post marker (`docs/reviews/2026-11-18-whole-range/STOP-C3.md`, `STOP-C3V.md`, `review-c3v-operator-text/`). (3) A deploy that fails its canary must not be allowed to roll back to `619abda7` on a live 2027 box (that code reads every 2027 date as zero days left and rewrites state the new code then refuses): stop outward sending and page instead (Eric's decision pending, W12). (4) **Change sets H and H2 (2026-11-25) deploy together, and a rollback past H2 needs a check first.** H makes the policy play every day from streak 57; H2 lets the state checks accept a streak or best above 57 (up to 400). Never deploy code that has H without H2: after a hit at 57 the fetch would refuse MLB's 58 and the old 57 would stay in use with no alert for 14 hours. Before reverting to any code older than H2, have the lead verify the ACTIVE and the BEST streak in both observation files (`contest_streak.json`, `contest_streak.manual.json`) and in any pending pick's `chosen_on`: the older code refuses a file holding a value above 57, and an expired dated observation holding one can block a valid automatic observation. Where the older code can represent the current state, replace the files with verified current state; get a fresh selection for a pending pick whose metadata it cannot read. Picks already committed stay scoreable. | Eric / Claude | `docs/reviews/2026-11-18-whole-range/FINDINGS.md` |
